    <statement><p>Use polynomial fitting to find the formula for the <m>n</m>th term of the sequence <m>(a_n)_{n \ge 0}</m> which starts,</p>
<p><me>{-1, 4, 18, 50, 109, 204}, \ldots</me></p>
<p><m>a_n =</m> <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left({\frac{3}{2}}\right)n^{3}+\left({\frac{7}{2}}\right)n-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>a_n = {\left({\frac{3}{2}}\right)n^{3}+\left({\frac{7}{2}}\right)n-1}\text{.}</m> Here we know that we are looking for a cubic because the third differences are constant. So <m>a_n = an^3 + bn^2 + cn + d\text{.}</m> Since <m>a_0 = {-1}</m>, we know <m>d= {-1}\text{.}</m> So just solve the system</p>
<p><me>\begin{aligned}
{4} \amp  = a + b + c + {-1}\\
{18} \amp  = 8a + 4b + 2c + {-1}\\
{50} \amp  = 27a + 9b + 3c + {-1}\\
\end{aligned}</me></p>
<p>to find <m>a = {{\frac{3}{2}}}</m>, <m>b = 0</m>, and <m>c = {{\frac{7}{2}}}</m>.</p>
</solution>
